african allied forces ( ecomog ) , my country relied heavily on the foreign
earning generated from diamond trade . this money was personally kept by
the then president , major johnny koroma , since our banking system had
collapsed during the war .
however , as the war progressed , it became apparent that we were going
to lose the war to the superior and better armed west african allied
forces ( ecomog ) . at this point , the key officers of the administration
started making frantic efforts on how to leave sierra leone safely ,
thereby sharing the proceeds / money from the diamond trade . my father was
one of the key officers who succeeded in getting the sum of us $ 20 . 5
million ( twenty million , five hundred thousand united states dollars cash ) .
we made arrangements and transferred the money through diplomatic means
to south africa where i and my family lives for good three years ,
unfortunately , my father died of heart attack after two years of exile in
