news :
london ( reuters ) - - march 31 , 2 oo 5 - - oil markets have entered a
` ` super - spike ' ' period that could see 197 o ' s - style price surges as high as
$ 1 o 5 a barrel , investment bank goldman sachs said in a research report .
goldman ' s global investment research note also raised the bank ' s 2005
and 2 oo 6 new york mercantile exchange crude price forecasts to $ 5 o and
$ 55 respectively , from $ 41 and $ 40 .
these forecasts sit at the top of a table of predictions from 25
analysts , consultants and government bodies surveyed by reuters .
` ` we believe oil markets may have entered the early stages of what we
have referred to as a ` ` super spike ' ' period - - a multi - year trading
band of oil prices high enough to meaningfully reduce energy consumption
and recreate a spare capacity cushion only after which will lower energy
prices return , ' ' goldman ' s analysts wrote .
c o m p a n y o v e r v i e w
bnp petroleum corporation , inc . is an irving based oil and gas
exploration and development ( e bpet ) , an independent oil and
gas company , announced today restarting of "" hooks "" lease located in
wichita county texas , after accomplishing modifications and upgrades on
some wells , in the last few months . the shallow wells previously had been
producing oil and water at low rates due to low bottom pressure , which
